// @check
// @error a `type` declaration may not take the built-in type name `u8`
// D1585 — `u8` IS A BUILT-IN TYPE NAME, and the reserved-name screen did not know it.
//
// The screen asked `primTyOfName`, which deliberately WITHHOLDS `u8` (the storage type is
// reachable only as an array element, never as a value), so `type u8` slipped through where
// `type i32` and `type f64` did not — while the merge's own copy of the same question
// (`modNameIsBuiltinTy`) did include `u8`. Two copies, two answers. `isBuiltinTyName` is now
// the one home and both readers ask it.
//
// The SET is what this pins, not the sentence: a name an annotation resolves with no `type`
// in sight may not be redeclared, and `u8` is such a name even though it is not a primitive.
type u8 = { x: i32 }

print(1)
